 and new visualization tools</article-title><source>Nucleic Acids Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>213</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9399837</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Michaels</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Tchou</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Grollman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A repair system for 8-oxo-7,8-dihydrodeoxyguanine</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>1992</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>10964</fpage><lpage>10968</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1445834</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grollman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Moriya</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mutagensis by 8-oxoguanine: An enemy within</article-title><source>Trends Genet</source><year>1993</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>246</fpage><lpage>249</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8379000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rosenquist</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Zharkow</surname><given-names>DO</given-names></name><name><surname>Grollman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloning and characterization of a mammalian 8-oxoguanine DNA glycosylase</article-title><source>P Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>1997</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>5197</fpage><lpage>5202</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fromme</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Banerjee</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Huang</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Verdine</surname><given-names>GL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural basis for removal of adenine mispaired with 8-oxoguanine by MutY adenine DNA glycosylase</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2004</year><volume>427</volume><fpage>652</fpage><lpage>656</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14961129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Prasad</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Grollman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>8-OxodGTP incorporation by DNA polymerase &#x003b2; is modified by active site residue Asn279</article-title><source>Biochemistry</source><year>2000</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>1029</fpage><lpage>1033</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10653647</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freisinger</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Grollman</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kisker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lesion (in)tolerance reveals insights into DNA replication fidelity</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><year>2004</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>1494</fpage><lpage>1505</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15057282</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rechkoblit</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Malinina</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuryavyi</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Broyde</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Geacintov</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Patel</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stepwise translocation of Dpo4 polymerase during error-free bypass of an oxoG lesion</article-title><source>PLos Biology</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>42</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brieba</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokoska</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Bebenek</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kunkel</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellenberger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A lysine residue in the fingers subdomain of T7 DNA polymerase modulates the miscoding potential of 8-oxo-7,8-dihydroguanosine</article-title><source>Structure</source><year>2005</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>1653</fpage><lpage>1659</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16271888</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brieba</surname><given-names>LG</given-names></name><name><surname>Eichman</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kokoska</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Doublie</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kunkel</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Ellenberger</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural basis for the dual coding of potential of 8-oxoguanosine by a high-fidelity DNA polymerase</article-